- `sphgen` clustering: 21 vs 20 clusters (algorithmic sensitivity at cluster boundary)

If bitwise reproducibility is required, remove `-ffast-math` from CFLAGS/CXXFLAGS/OCFLAGS and rebuild.

## Compiler Optimization Pass (Sat 16 May 2026)

### Replace `-ffast-math` with Safer Flags
`-ffast-math` suspected of slightly lowering runtime success rates. Removed from all 4 flag variables (CFLAGS, CXXFLAGS, FFLAGS, OCFLAGS). Replaced with IEEE-result-preserving safe subset:
- `-fno-math-errno` — math functions won't set errno (safe inlines)
- `-fno-trapping-math` — no FP exception handlers (safe)
- Removed dangerous sub-flags: `-ffinite-math-only`, `-funsafe-math-optimizations`, `-fassociative-math`, `-freciprocal-math`

### Added Register Allocation & CSE Optimizations
- `-fweb` — splits register lifetimes for better allocation
- `-fira-loop-pressure` — loop-aware register allocation
- `-fgcse-after-reload` — catches CSE opportunities after register allocation
- `-fsplit-paths` — optimizes if-then-else chains

### Added Loop Nest & Graphite Optimizations
- `-floop-nest-optimize` — polyhedral loop nest optimization
- `-fpeel-loops` — peels loop prologue/epilogue
- `-fsplit-loops` — splits loops with multiple exits
- `-floop-unroll-and-jam` — outer loop unrolling + inner loop jamming

Applied identically to CFLAGS, CXXFLAGS, FFLAGS, and OCFLAGS.

### Created PGO Build Script (`install/pgo_build.sh`)
Three-phase profile-guided optimization process using the test suite as training workload:
- **Phase 1** (`-fprofile-generate=/tmp/dock6_pgo_gcda` via DOCKBUILDFLAGS): Builds instrumented binaries
- **Phase 2** (`make test`): Runs test suite as training workload, collecting profile data
- **Phase 3** (`-fprofile-use -fprofile-correction`): Deletes .o files, rebuilds optimized binaries using profile data

### PGO Build Attempt — Fortran linking issue
Phase 1 instrumentation build failed at `nchemgrid_GB` link step: `gfortran-15` didn't auto-link `libgcov` (undefined `___gcov_exit`, etc.). Root cause: several Fortran utility Makefiles (`gbsa_grids/schemgrid_GB/SA/Makefile`, etc.) use `$(FC) $(FFLAGS) $(OBJS) -o $@` for linking but omit `$(DOCKBUILDFLAGS)`. The `-lgcov` library was never linked despite being in DOCKBUILDFLAGS.

### Revised Approach — dock6-only PGO
Switched to building only the dock6 binary with PGO instrumentation. Utilities are built normally (without PGO) in the same phase 1 build. This avoids the Fortran Makefile issue entirely.

Usage:
```bash
cd install && ./pgo_build.sh      # PGO build (dock6 only)
cd install && ./pgo_build.sh clean  # Remove PGO artifacts
```

